can take years.

292
00:09:18,979 --> 00:09:19,704
When you buy,

293
00:09:19,704 --> 00:09:20,708
you start with it.

294
00:09:20,888 --> 00:09:23,515
A strong reputation brings in new customers

295
00:09:23,515 --> 00:09:26,020
through word of mouth and makes marketing

296
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:27,181
far more effective.

297
00:09:27,531 --> 00:09:29,516
But reputation is fragile.

298
00:09:29,696 --> 00:09:32,165
Check reviews carefully before buying,

299
00:09:32,165 --> 00:09:34,440
because a bad reputation is hard to

300
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:34,700
fix.

301
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,015
And after buying,

302
00:09:36,015 --> 00:09:39,152
protect the reputation by keeping quality high.

303
00:09:39,332 --> 00:09:41,677
Customers don't care that the owner changed.

304
00:09:41,857 --> 00:09:43,807
They care whether the service is still

305
00:09:43,807 --> 00:09:44,063
good.

306
00:09:44,414 --> 00:09:45,354
Reason 9.

307
00:09:45,534 --> 00:09:47,183
Real data to decide with.

308
00:09:47,363 --> 00:09:49,109
you can see the numbers before you

309
00:09:49,109 --> 00:09:49,418
commit

310
00:09:49,768 --> 00:09:50,615
Reason nine.

311
00:09:50,795 --> 00:09:51,527
Real data.

312
00:09:51,707 --> 00:09:53,761
A startup runs on predictions.

313
00:09:53,941 --> 00:09:56,077
You guess how many customers you'll get

314
00:09:56,077 --> 00:09:57,227
and what they'll pay.

315
00:09:57,407 --> 00:09:59,093
When you buy a business,

316
00:09:59,093 --> 00:10:01,129
you can look at real numbers:

317
00:10:01,129 --> 00:10:02,183
years of sales,

318
00:10:02,183 --> 00:10:05,975
costs, profits, customer counts and seasonal patterns.

319
00:10:06,326 --> 00:10:08,521
That data helps you decide whether the

320
00:10:08,521 --> 00:10:09,561
price makes sense,

321
00:10:09,561 --> 00:10:11,871
whether the business can support a loan,

322
00:10:11,871 --> 00:10:13,431
and where it could improve.

323
00:10:13,611 --> 00:10:15,503
It replaces hope with evidence.

324
00:10:15,683 --> 00:10:16,977
Lenders use it too,

325
00:10:16,977 --> 00:10:19,224
which is why financing is easier.

326
00:10:19,575 --> 00:10:21,606
The key is to verify the data.

327
00:10:21,786 --> 00:10:24,609
Compare the profit and loss statements with

328
00:10:24,609 --> 00:10:26,709
tax returns and bank statements.

329
00:10:26,889 --> 00:10:29,002
Have an accountant review everything.

330
00:10:29,182 --> 00:10:32,270
Sellers sometimes present their numbers in the

331
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:33,612
best possible light,

332
00:10:33,612 --> 00:10:35,022
so trust, but verify.

333
00:10:35,372 --> 00:10:36,347
Reason 10.

334
00:10:36,527 --> 00:10:38,257
Baby boomer retirements.

335
00:10:38,437 --> 00:10:41,006
a generation of owners is getting ready

336
00:10:41,006 --> 00:10:41,467
to sell

337
00:10:41,817 --> 00:10:42,711
Reason ten.

338
00:10:42,891 --> 00:10:43,622
Timing.

339
00:10:43,802 --> 00:10:46,731
A large share of small business owners

340
00:10:46,731 --> 00:10:49,969
in America are baby boomers approaching or

341
00:10:49,969 --> 00:10:51,511
past retirement age.

342
00:10:51,691 --> 00:10:53,641
Many of them don't have children who

343
00:10:53,641 --> 00:10:54,617
want to take over.

344
00:10:54,797 --> 00:10:57,326
That means many profitable businesses may be

345
00:10:57,326 --> 00:10:59,568
looking for buyers in the coming years.

346
00:10:59,919 --> 00:11:02,431
For buyers, that can mean more choice

347
00:11:02,431 --> 00:11:03,721
and, in some cases,

348
00:11:03,721 --> 00:11:05,282
more motivated sellers.

349
00:11:05,462 --> 00:11:07,806
A retiring owner who has spent thirty

350
00:11:07,806 --> 00:11:10,529
years building a business often cares about

351
00:11:10,529 --> 00:11:11,670
who takes it over,

352
00:11:11,670 --> 00:11:14,266
about protecting employees and customers,

353
00:11:14,266 --> 00:11:16,863
not just about getting the highest price.

354
00:11:17,214 --> 00:11:19,431
This doesn't mean bargains are everywhere.

355
00:11:19,611 --> 00:11:22,254
Good businesses still sell for fair prices,

356
00:11:22,254 --> 00:11:24,836
and competition from investors is growing.

357
00:11:25,016 --> 00:11:27,299
But the wave of retirements is one

358
00:11:27,299 --> 00:11:30,053
reason many people believe this decade is

359
00:11:30,053 --> 00:11:31,934
a strong time to buy a small

360
00:11:31,934 --> 00:11:32,539
business.

361
00:11:32,889 --> 00:11:33,875
Reason 11.

362
00:11:34,055 --> 00:11:35,913
Lower total cost of risk.

363
00:11:36,093 --> 00:11:38,299
starting can cost more than it looks

364
00:11:38,649 --> 00:11:39,624
Reason eleven.

365
00:11:39,804 --> 00:11:41,778
The true cost of starting is often

366
00:11:41,778 --> 00:11:42,997
higher than it looks.

367
00:11:43,177 --> 00:11:45,338
Startups spend on equipment,

368
00:11:45,338 --> 00:11:47,963
buildout, marketing and inventory,

369
00:11:47,963 --> 00:11:50,897
then often lose money for months while

370
00:11:50,897 --> 00:11:52,441
they find customers.

371
00:11:52,621 --> 00:11:54,858
Add the cost of the founder's unpaid

372
00:11:54,858 --> 00:11:57,094
time, and the real price of starting

373
00:11:57,094 --> 00:11:58,647
can be surprisingly high.

374
00:11:58,997 --> 00:12:01,543
Buying looks more expensive up front because

375
00:12:01,543 --> 00:12:02,932
you pay for the profits.

376
00:12:03,112 --> 00:12:05,005
But you're paying for something proven.

377
00:12:05,185 --> 00:12:07,023
When you compare the total cost,

378
00:12:07,023 --> 00:12:09,322
including the money lost while a startup

379
00:12:09,322 --> 00:12:10,988
ramps up and the risk that it

380
00:12:10,988 --> 00:12:12,080
never works at all,

381
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,976
buying can be the cheaper path to

382
00:12:13,976 --> 00:12:15,355
a given level of income.

383
00:12:15,705 --> 00:12:17,260
Here's a simple illustration.

384
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,746
A startup might need one hundred fifty

385
00:12:19,746 --> 00:12:22,173
thousand dollars and two years of little

386
00:12:22,173 --> 00:12:24,114
or no income before it earns one

387
00:12:24,114 --> 00:12:25,571
hundred thousand a year,

388
00:12:25,571 --> 00:12:26,299
if it works.

389
00:12:26,479 --> 00:12:29,442
An existing business earning one hundred thousand

390
00:12:29,442 --> 00:12:31,499
might cost three hundred thousand,

391
00:12:31,499 --> 00:12:32,890
but pay from month one,

392
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:35,128
with a much higher chance of success.

393
00:12:35,308 --> 00:12:37,793
Different paths, very different risks.

394
00:12:38,143 --> 00:12:39,106
Reason 12.

395
00:12:39,286 --> 00:12:40,505
Room to improve.

396
00:12:40,685 --> 00:12:43,263
many small businesses are under-managed

397
00:12:43,613 --> 00:12:44,692
Reason twelve.

398
00:12:44,872 --> 00:12:46,173
Room to improve.

399
00:12:46,353 --> 00:12:48,893
Many small businesses are run the same

400
00:12:48,893 --> 00:12:49,963
way for decades.

401
00:12:50,143 --> 00:12:52,454
Prices haven't been raised in years.

402
00:12:52,634 --> 00:12:54,515
Marketing is word of mouth only.

403
00:12:54,695 --> 00:12:56,633
Nobody answers the phone after five.

404
00:12:56,813 --> 00:12:59,495
The website looks like it's from 2005.

405
00:12:59,846 --> 00:13:01,807
For a buyer with fresh energy,

406
00:13:01,807 --> 00:13:03,572
that can be an opportunity.

407
00:13:03,752 --> 00:13:06,786
Modest improvements, like better pricing,

408
00:13:06,786 --> 00:13:09,745
online booking, a few marketing efforts,

409
00:13:09,745 --> 00:13:11,002
or a new service,

410
00:13:11,002 --> 00:13:13,296
can raise profits meaningfully.

411
00:13:13,476 --> 00:13:15,922
And because businesses are often valued as

412
00:13:15,922 --> 00:13:17,145
a multiple of profit,

413
00:13:17,145 --> 00:13:19,300
higher profit can also raise what the

414
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,349
business is worth.

415
00:13:20,699 --> 00:13:22,605
Be careful not to change too much

416
00:13:22,605 --> 00:13:23,125
too fast.

417
00:13:23,305 --> 00:13:25,801
Customers and employees may resist.

418
00:13:25,981 --> 00:13:28,575
The best buyers learn the business first,

419
00:13:28,575 --> 00:13:29,587
keep what works,

420
00:13:29,587 --> 00:13:31,612
and make improvements gradually.

421
00:13:31,792 --> 00:13:33,882
But the upside of improving an under

422
00:13:33,882 --> 00:13:35,914
managed business is one of the most

423
00:13:35,914 --> 00:13:37,365
exciting parts of buying.

424
00:13:37,715 --> 00:13:38,968
Reason 13.

425
00:13:39,148 --> 00:13:40,368
Training from the seller.

426
00:13:40,548 --> 00:13:42,382
the previous owner can teach you

427
00:13:42,732 --> 00:13:44,032
Reason thirteen.

428
00:13:44,212 --> 00:13:45,512
Training from the seller.

429
00:13:45,692 --> 00:13:49,044
Many purchase agreements include a transition period

430
00:13:49,044 --> 00:13:51,300
where the seller stays for weeks or

431
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,976
months to train the buyer,

432
00:13:52,976 --> 00:13:55,426
introduce key customers and suppliers,

433
00:13:55,426 --> 00:13:56,780
and answer questions.

434
00:13:57,130 --> 00:13:59,591
That's like getting a private apprenticeship from

435
00:13:59,591 --> 00:14:01,600
the person who knows the business better

436
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,203
than anyone.

437
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:04,612
When a seller is also financing part

438
00:14:04,612 --> 00:14:05,355
of the deal,

439
00:14:05,355 --> 00:14:07,399
they have an extra reason to help

440
00:14:07,399 --> 00:14:09,690
you succeed, because they want to get

441
00:14:09,690 --> 00:14:09,999
paid.

442
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:13,260
Negotiate the training period clearly in the

443
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:14,517
contract: how long,

444
00:14:14,517 --> 00:14:15,509
how many hours,

445
00:14:15,509 --> 00:14:16,898
and what it includes.

446
00:14:17,078 --> 00:14:19,670
Some deals also include a non compete

447
00:14:19,670 --> 00:14:23,103
agreement, which prevents the seller from opening

448
00:14:23,103 --> 00:14:25,065
a competing business nearby.

449
00:14:25,416 --> 00:14:26,681
Reason 14.

450
00:14:26,861 --> 00:14:28,161
Faster path to scale.

451
00:14:28,341 --> 00:14:31,197
build on something instead of from nothing

452
00:14:31,548 --> 00:14:32,836
Reason fourteen.

453
00:14:33,016 --> 00:14:34,630
A faster path to scale.

454
00:14:34,810 --> 00:14:37,339
Once you own one profitable business and

455
00:14:37,339 --> 00:14:39,868
understand it, you can grow by improving

456
00:14:39,868 --> 00:14:41,195
it, adding locations,

457
00:14:41,195 --> 00:14:43,471
or buying similar businesses nearby.

458
00:14:43,651 --> 00:14:47,424
Some owners eventually combine several small businesses

459
00:14:47,424 --> 00:14:48,934
into a larger company.

460
00:14:49,284 --> 00:14:52,579
Larger, combined businesses can sometimes sell for

461
00:14:52,579 --> 00:14:54,755
higher multiples than small ones,

462
00:14:54,755 --> 00:14:57,194
because buyers see them as less risky

463
00:14:57,194 --> 00:14:59,303
and less dependent on one owner.

464
00:14:59,483 --> 00:15:02,467
That's one reason investors buy small businesses

465
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:03,338
and grow them.

466
00:15:03,688 --> 00:15:06,481
This is an advanced strategy that requires

467
00:15:06,481 --> 00:15:09,075
management skill and careful financing.

468
00:15:09,255 --> 00:15:11,478
But it shows how buying one business

469
00:15:11,478 --> 00:15:14,010
can become the foundation for much bigger

470
00:15:14,010 --> 00:15:15,060
wealth over time.

471
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:16,594
Reason 15.

472
00:15:16,774 --> 00:15:18,399
Ownership without inventing.

473
00:15:18,579 --> 00:15:20,414
you don't need a brilliant idea

474
00:15:20,764 --> 00:15:22,168
And reason fifteen.

475
00:15:22,348 --> 00:15:24,206
You don't need a brilliant idea.

476
00:15:24,386 --> 00:15:26,930
Many people never become business owners because

477
00:15:26,930 --> 00:15:28,891
they're waiting for the perfect idea.

478
00:15:29,071 --> 00:15:30,708
Buying removes that barrier.

479
00:15:30,888 --> 00:15:32,699
You don't need to invent anything.

480
00:15:32,879 --> 00:15:34,353
You need to run something well.

481
00:15:34,704 --> 00:15:37,365
That opens ownership to people who are

482
00:15:37,365 --> 00:15:38,696
good at operations,

483
00:15:38,696 --> 00:15:41,358
management, sales or customer service,

484
00:15:41,358 --> 00:15:43,109
but who aren't inventors.

485
00:15:43,289 --> 00:15:46,167
Some of the most successful small business

486
00:15:46,167 --> 00:15:49,525
owners are simply excellent operators of ordinary

487
00:15:49,525 --> 00:15:50,278
businesses.

488
00:15:50,629 --> 00:15:52,610
Ordinary businesses, run well,

489
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:55,516
can produce extraordinary results over time.

490
00:15:55,696 --> 00:15:57,218
A plumbing company,

491
00:15:57,218 --> 00:15:58,740
an accounting firm,

492
00:15:58,740 --> 00:15:59,621
a car wash.

493
00:15:59,801 --> 00:16:01,995
None of these require genius.

494
00:16:02,175 --> 00:16:03,828
They require consistency,

495
00:16:03,828 --> 00:16:06,540
good people and careful money management.

496
00:16:06,891 --> 00:16:08,085
Now, to be fair,

497
00:16:08,085 --> 00:16:10,548
buying a business has real risks.

498
00:16:10,728 --> 00:16:12,609
Let's go through the biggest ones.

499
00:16:12,959 --> 00:16:13,713
Risk one.

500
00:16:13,893 --> 00:16:14,810
Overpaying.

501
00:16:14,990 --> 00:16:16,131
If you pay too much,

502
00:16:16,131 --> 00:16:18,412
the business may not produce enough cash

503
00:16:18,412 --> 00:16:20,122
to repay the loan and pay you.

504
00:16:20,302 --> 00:16:21,208
Risk two.

505
00:16:21,388 --> 00:16:24,117
Hidden problems: declining sales,

506
00:16:24,117 --> 00:16:28,005
unpaid taxes, legal disputes or equipment about

507
00:16:28,005 --> 00:16:28,667
to fail.

508
00:16:28,847 --> 00:16:30,020
Risk three.

509
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,131
Customer or employee loss after the sale,

510
00:16:33,131 --> 00:16:36,420
especially if the business depended heavily on

511
00:16:36,420 --> 00:16:38,350
the seller's relationships.

512
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:39,512
Risk four.

513
00:16:39,692 --> 00:16:39,866
Debt.

514
00:16:40,046 --> 00:16:41,946
A loan has to be paid even

515
00:16:41,946 --> 00:16:42,969
in bad months,

516
00:16:42,969 --> 00:16:45,672
and many SBA loans require a personal

517
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:48,813
guarantee, which can put personal assets at

518
00:16:48,813 --> 00:16:50,786
risk if the business fails.

519
00:16:50,966 --> 00:16:51,929
Risk five.

520
00:16:52,109 --> 00:16:53,270
You might not enjoy it.

521
00:16:53,450 --> 00:16:55,174
Owning a business is demanding,

522
00:16:55,174 --> 00:16:57,398
and buying one doesn't make that easier.

523
00:16:57,578 --> 00:16:59,668
Know what daily life looks like before

524
00:16:59,668 --> 00:17:00,109
you buy.

525
00:17:00,459 --> 00:17:01,106
To be fair,

526
00:17:01,106 --> 00:17:03,634
starting a business is sometimes the better

527
00:17:03,634 --> 00:17:04,046
choice.

528
00:17:04,226 --> 00:17:04,876
Here's when.

529
00:17:05,227 --> 00:17:07,579
Starting makes sense when you have very

530
00:17:07,579 --> 00:17:10,052
little capital and the business can begin

531
00:17:10,052 --> 00:17:11,983
small, like a service you can do

532
00:17:11,983 --> 00:17:13,551
yourself with basic tools.

533
00:17:13,731 --> 00:17:15,607
It makes sense when you have a

534
00:17:15,607 --> 00:17:17,796
genuinely new idea or a market that

535
00:17:17,796 --> 00:17:19,548
no existing business serves.

536
00:17:19,728 --> 00:17:21,496
And it makes sense when you want

537
00:17:21,496 --> 00:17:23,707
to build something with your own culture

538
00:17:23,707 --> 00:17:25,089
and methods from day one,

539
00:17:25,089 --> 00:17:27,355
without inheriting someone else's habits.

540
00:17:27,706 --> 00:17:29,998
Starting can also be a great way

541
00:17:29,998 --> 00:17:30,643
to learn.

542
00:17:30,823 --> 00:17:33,339
Many people start a small side business

543
00:17:33,339 --> 00:17:35,468
to discover what they're good at,

544
00:17:35,468 --> 00:17:37,727
then later buy a larger business in

545
00:17:37,727 --> 00:17:38,694
the same field.

546
00:17:38,874 --> 00:17:40,651
The two paths aren't enemies.

547
00:17:40,831 --> 00:17:41,876
For many owners,

548
00:17:41,876 --> 00:17:44,098
starting small teaches the skills,

549
00:17:44,098 --> 00:17:46,450
and buying later provides the scale.

550
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,529
The honest answer is this.

551
00:17:48,709 --> 00:17:50,151
If you have the capital,

552
00:17:50,151 --> 00:17:52,554
the credit and the temperament to manage

553
00:17:52,554 --> 00:17:55,136
people, buying often offers better odds and

554
00:17:55,136 --> 00:17:55,977
faster income.

555
00:17:56,157 --> 00:17:58,416
If you have little money but plenty

556
00:17:58,416 --> 00:17:59,642
of time and energy,

557
00:17:59,642 --> 00:18:02,287
starting small may be the realistic path.

558
00:18:02,467 --> 00:18:04,046
Know which one describes you.

559
00:18:04,397 --> 00:18:07,009
Let's make this concrete with three made

560
00:18:07,009 --> 00:18:08,576
up but realistic buyers.

561
00:18:08,927 --> 00:18:10,979
Buyer one is a forty year old

562
00:18:10,979 --> 00:18:14,023
operations manager tired of corporate life.

563
00:18:14,203 --> 00:18:16,947
She has eighty thousand dollars saved and

564
00:18:16,947 --> 00:18:17,884
strong credit.

565
00:18:18,064 --> 00:18:20,708
She spends six months looking at listings

566
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:23,675
and buys a commercial cleaning company earning

567
00:18:23,675 --> 00:18:26,254
about one hundred ten thousand dollars a

568
00:18:26,254 --> 00:18:27,738
year, with an SBA loan,

569
00:18:27,738 --> 00:18:30,511
seller financing and a three month training

570
00:18:30,511 --> 00:18:30,962
period.

571
00:18:31,142 --> 00:18:33,613
Her management experience turns out to be

572
00:18:33,613 --> 00:18:35,601
exactly what the business needed.

573
00:18:35,951 --> 00:18:38,089
Buyer two is a thirty two year

574
00:18:38,089 --> 00:18:39,515
old HVAC technician.

575
00:18:39,695 --> 00:18:41,692
He knows the trade inside and out

576
00:18:41,692 --> 00:18:43,387
but has never run a company.

577
00:18:43,567 --> 00:18:46,335
When his boss announces plans to retire,

578
00:18:46,335 --> 00:18:48,134
the two of them agree on a

579
00:18:48,134 --> 00:18:50,833
sale with significant seller financing,

