867
00:27:57,564 --> 00:28:00,733
People compare prices instead of comparing outcomes.

868
00:28:01,083 --> 00:28:03,034
The third reason is not knowing it's

869
00:28:03,034 --> 00:28:03,522
possible.

870
00:28:03,702 --> 00:28:06,225
Most people have never heard of SBA

871
00:28:06,225 --> 00:28:10,261
acquisition loans, seller financing or business brokers.

872
00:28:10,441 --> 00:28:12,346
They simply don't know that buying a

873
00:28:12,346 --> 00:28:14,516
business is an option for regular people.

874
00:28:14,696 --> 00:28:15,590
Now you do.

875
00:28:15,940 --> 00:28:18,216
The fourth reason is fear of debt.

876
00:28:18,396 --> 00:28:21,370
Borrowing hundreds of thousands of dollars feels

877
00:28:21,370 --> 00:28:23,539
terrifying, and caution is healthy.

878
00:28:23,719 --> 00:28:26,601
But there's a difference between debt used

879
00:28:26,601 --> 00:28:28,659
for a car that loses value and

880
00:28:28,659 --> 00:28:30,717
debt used to buy an asset that

881
00:28:30,717 --> 00:28:33,530
produces cash and repays the loan itself.

882
00:28:33,710 --> 00:28:35,962
The question isn't whether debt is scary.

883
00:28:36,142 --> 00:28:38,652
It's whether the business can comfortably carry

884
00:28:38,652 --> 00:28:39,880
it, even in a bad year.

885
00:28:40,231 --> 00:28:42,135
The fifth reason is ego.

886
00:28:42,315 --> 00:28:44,636
Some people want the business to be

887
00:28:44,636 --> 00:28:46,825
entirely theirs, built their way,

888
00:28:46,825 --> 00:28:48,085
from the ground up.

889
00:28:48,265 --> 00:28:49,751
That's a valid choice.

890
00:28:49,931 --> 00:28:52,307
But it's worth asking honestly whether you

891
00:28:52,307 --> 00:28:53,664
want to build something,

892
00:28:53,664 --> 00:28:55,587
or whether you want the income and

893
00:28:55,587 --> 00:28:57,454
freedom that ownership can bring.

894
00:28:57,634 --> 00:28:58,710
If it's the second,

895
00:28:58,710 --> 00:29:00,862
buying may get you there years sooner.

896
00:29:01,212 --> 00:29:02,001
The takeaway.

897
00:29:02,181 --> 00:29:03,981
Starting is more romantic.

898
00:29:04,161 --> 00:29:06,053
Buying is often more rational.

899
00:29:06,233 --> 00:29:08,393
Choose based on the outcome you want,

900
00:29:08,393 --> 00:29:10,204
not the story you want to tell.

901
00:29:10,554 --> 00:29:11,424
Third angle.

902
00:29:11,604 --> 00:29:12,405
The playbook.

903
00:29:12,585 --> 00:29:14,513
How do you actually buy a business?

904
00:29:14,862 --> 00:29:15,559
Step one.

905
00:29:15,739 --> 00:29:17,214
Get your finances ready.

906
00:29:17,394 --> 00:29:18,695
Know your credit score,

907
00:29:18,695 --> 00:29:20,618
savings and how much you could put

908
00:29:20,618 --> 00:29:22,711
down while keeping an emergency fund.

909
00:29:22,891 --> 00:29:23,773
Step two.

910
00:29:23,953 --> 00:29:26,691
Choose industries that fit your skills and

911
00:29:26,691 --> 00:29:27,343
interests.

912
00:29:27,523 --> 00:29:28,429
Step three.

913
00:29:28,609 --> 00:29:31,180
Search for businesses through brokers,

914
00:29:31,180 --> 00:29:33,007
business for sale websites,

915
00:29:33,007 --> 00:29:35,781
your local network and even by contacting

916
00:29:35,781 --> 00:29:36,864
owners directly.

917
00:29:37,214 --> 00:29:38,049
Step four.

918
00:29:38,229 --> 00:29:39,739
Analyze the numbers.

919
00:29:39,919 --> 00:29:41,866
Ask for at least three years of

920
00:29:41,866 --> 00:29:44,568
tax returns, profit and loss statements and

921
00:29:44,568 --> 00:29:45,573
bank statements.

922
00:29:45,753 --> 00:29:46,774
Step five.

923
00:29:46,954 --> 00:29:47,832
Make an offer,

924
00:29:47,832 --> 00:29:49,525
usually a letter of intent,

925
00:29:49,525 --> 00:29:51,845
that sets the price and terms subject

926
00:29:51,845 --> 00:29:52,910
to due diligence.

927
00:29:53,090 --> 00:29:54,124
Step six.

928
00:29:54,304 --> 00:29:56,960
Do the due diligence with an accountant

929
00:29:56,960 --> 00:29:59,003
and lawyer: verify financials,

930
00:29:59,003 --> 00:30:00,910
review leases and contracts,

931
00:30:00,910 --> 00:30:03,975
inspect equipment, and talk to key employees.

932
00:30:04,325 --> 00:30:05,277
Step seven.

933
00:30:05,457 --> 00:30:08,019
Arrange financing with an SBA lender or

934
00:30:08,019 --> 00:30:11,238
bank, and negotiate seller financing if possible.

935
00:30:11,418 --> 00:30:12,161
Step eight.

936
00:30:12,341 --> 00:30:15,093
Close, then manage the transition carefully.

937
00:30:15,273 --> 00:30:17,856
Keep employees and customers informed,

938
00:30:17,856 --> 00:30:19,488
learn before you change,

939
00:30:19,488 --> 00:30:22,343
and use the seller's training period well.

940
00:30:22,694 --> 00:30:24,442
Throughout all eight steps,

941
00:30:24,442 --> 00:30:26,644
build your team of advisors early:

942
00:30:26,644 --> 00:30:30,401
an accountant who understands small business acquisitions,

943
00:30:30,401 --> 00:30:33,315
a lawyer who has handled purchase agreements,

944
00:30:33,315 --> 00:30:35,906
and a lender experienced with SBA deals.

945
00:30:36,086 --> 00:30:38,141
Their fees are small compared with the

946
00:30:38,141 --> 00:30:39,331
price of the business,

947
00:30:39,331 --> 00:30:41,278
and the mistakes they help you avoid

948
00:30:41,278 --> 00:30:42,955
can be worth far more than they

949
00:30:42,955 --> 00:30:43,226
cost.

950
00:30:43,576 --> 00:30:45,886
And give yourself permission to walk away.

951
00:30:46,066 --> 00:30:48,408
Most serious buyers look at dozens of

952
00:30:48,408 --> 00:30:51,194
businesses and make offers on several before

953
00:30:51,194 --> 00:30:52,080
one works out.

954
00:30:52,260 --> 00:30:54,610
Walking away from a bad deal isn't

955
00:30:54,610 --> 00:30:55,162
failure.

956
00:30:55,342 --> 00:30:57,556
It's the most important skill a buyer

957
00:30:57,556 --> 00:30:58,094
can have.

958
00:30:58,443 --> 00:30:59,256
Question one.

959
00:30:59,436 --> 00:31:00,980
How much money do I need?

960
00:31:01,160 --> 00:31:02,882
It depends on the price,

961
00:31:02,882 --> 00:31:05,320
but SBA deals often require a down

962
00:31:05,320 --> 00:31:07,256
payment around ten percent,

963
00:31:07,256 --> 00:31:10,054
plus closing costs and working capital.

964
00:31:10,234 --> 00:31:13,182
Many buyers also keep personal reserves.

965
00:31:13,362 --> 00:31:14,268
Question two.

966
00:31:14,448 --> 00:31:16,120
Should I use a business broker?

967
00:31:16,300 --> 00:31:17,911
Brokers can help find deals,

968
00:31:17,911 --> 00:31:20,096
but they usually represent the seller.

969
00:31:20,276 --> 00:31:22,842
Your own accountant and lawyer represent you.

970
00:31:23,192 --> 00:31:24,214
Question three.

971
00:31:24,394 --> 00:31:26,774
What's a good first business to buy?

972
00:31:26,954 --> 00:31:29,391
Many first time buyers look for simple,

973
00:31:29,391 --> 00:31:32,516
steady businesses with recurring customers and low

974
00:31:32,516 --> 00:31:34,015
dependence on the owner,

975
00:31:34,015 --> 00:31:35,453
like service companies.

976
00:31:35,633 --> 00:31:36,643
Question four.

977
00:31:36,823 --> 00:31:38,808
Can I keep my job while buying?

978
00:31:38,988 --> 00:31:41,805
Some people buy businesses with managers in

979
00:31:41,805 --> 00:31:44,426
place, but most small businesses need an

980
00:31:44,426 --> 00:31:47,243
active owner, especially in the first year.

981
00:31:47,592 --> 00:31:48,579
Question five.

982
00:31:48,759 --> 00:31:50,187
What if my credit isn't great?

983
00:31:50,367 --> 00:31:52,187
SBA lenders look at credit,

984
00:31:52,187 --> 00:31:54,884
experience and the business's cash flow.

985
00:31:55,064 --> 00:31:57,833
Improving your credit and building savings for

986
00:31:57,833 --> 00:31:59,699
a year before buying can make a

987
00:31:59,699 --> 00:32:00,602
big difference.

988
00:32:00,782 --> 00:32:03,847
Seller financing can also help fill gaps.

989
00:32:04,027 --> 00:32:05,164
Question six.

990
00:32:05,344 --> 00:32:07,316
What if the seller won't show tax

991
00:32:07,316 --> 00:32:07,794
returns?

992
00:32:07,974 --> 00:32:08,717
Walk away.

993
00:32:08,897 --> 00:32:10,240
Without verified numbers,

994
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:12,067
you can't know what you're buying.

995
00:32:12,416 --> 00:32:13,392
Question seven.

996
00:32:13,572 --> 00:32:15,638
How long does buying a business take?

997
00:32:15,818 --> 00:32:18,117
From the first search to closing,

998
00:32:18,117 --> 00:32:20,346
many buyers take six months to a

999
00:32:20,346 --> 00:32:21,252
year or more.

1000
00:32:21,432 --> 00:32:23,870
Finding the right business takes time,

1001
00:32:23,870 --> 00:32:26,437
and due diligence and financing can take

1002
00:32:26,437 --> 00:32:27,399
several months.

1003
00:32:27,579 --> 00:32:29,587
Patience is part of the process,

1004
00:32:29,587 --> 00:32:31,782
and rushing is how mistakes happen.

1005
00:32:32,132 --> 00:32:34,129
Let's recap the fifteen reasons.

1006
00:32:34,309 --> 00:32:35,981
Cash flow from day one.

1007
00:32:36,161 --> 00:32:37,253
Proven survival.

1008
00:32:37,433 --> 00:32:38,977
Banks lend on history.

1009
00:32:39,157 --> 00:32:40,411
Seller financing.

1010
00:32:40,591 --> 00:32:41,740
Trained employees.

1011
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,522
Existing customers.

1012
00:32:43,702 --> 00:32:45,397
Systems and suppliers.

1013
00:32:45,577 --> 00:32:47,040
Brand and reputation.

1014
00:32:47,220 --> 00:32:48,091
Real data.

1015
00:32:48,271 --> 00:32:50,419
Retirements creating opportunities.

1016
00:32:50,599 --> 00:32:52,677
Lower total cost of risk.

1017
00:32:52,857 --> 00:32:54,238
Room to improve.

1018
00:32:54,418 --> 00:32:55,730
Training from the seller.

1019
00:32:55,910 --> 00:32:57,443
A faster path to scale.

1020
00:32:57,623 --> 00:33:00,537
And ownership without needing a brilliant idea.

1021
00:33:00,886 --> 00:33:02,233
And remember the risks.

1022
00:33:02,413 --> 00:33:04,377
Overpaying, hidden problems,

1023
00:33:04,377 --> 00:33:06,481
losing customers or employees,

1024
00:33:06,481 --> 00:33:08,585
debt with personal guarantees,

1025
00:33:08,585 --> 00:33:10,970
and simply not enjoying ownership.

1026
00:33:11,150 --> 00:33:13,427
The buyers who succeed are the ones

1027
00:33:13,427 --> 00:33:14,988
who respect those risks:

1028
00:33:14,988 --> 00:33:16,550
they verify the numbers,

1029
00:33:16,550 --> 00:33:19,477
keep reserves, negotiate help from the seller

1030
00:33:19,477 --> 00:33:21,494
and take the first year slowly.

1031
00:33:21,844 --> 00:33:23,876
Buying a business isn't a shortcut.

1032
00:33:24,056 --> 00:33:25,374
It's a different path,

1033
00:33:25,374 --> 00:33:27,351
one that trades a bigger check at

1034
00:33:27,351 --> 00:33:29,388
the start for a much better chance

1035
00:33:29,388 --> 00:33:30,047
of success.

1036
00:33:30,227 --> 00:33:31,453
For the right person,

1037
00:33:31,453 --> 00:33:33,556
with the right business at the right

1038
00:33:33,556 --> 00:33:35,132
price, it can be one of the

1039
00:33:35,132 --> 00:33:37,059
fastest ways to go from earning a

1040
00:33:37,059 --> 00:33:39,103
salary to owning an asset that pays

1041
00:33:39,103 --> 00:33:40,037
you for decades.

1042
00:33:40,387 --> 00:33:42,924
If buying a business sounds interesting,

1043
00:33:42,924 --> 00:33:43,685
start small.

